{"baseRefOid":"b279897aff455ac121c20ed107a91ad6ba23c010","body":"Protecting one additional resource previously repeated the pin's unchanged catalog in the journal. Version-2 resource deltas avoid that repetition. Staging registration now includes initial catalog protection and revalidates it before accessing storage; small-blob writers combine known blob, chunk, and loose physical identities before payload I/O.\n\nVersion-1 ledgers retain their original decoder and upgrade by atomic checkpoint on the first durable mutation. Older writers fail closed after upgrade. Required synchronization, acknowledgment ordering, GC arbitration, and retained-reader ownership remain intact.\n\nValidation at `01f406f` (rebased onto `b279897`):\n\n- Linux: 784 Rust tests; Clippy; 200 Python harness tests with two skips; real tmpfs disk-full recovery.\n- Both self-hosted Linux/macOS native CI test steps passed, as did 120 optimized permanent boundary samples per platform.\n- macOS real APFS disk-full recovery passed; checkpoint allocation may fail safely with `StorageFull`. Linux CI explicitly reports missing namespace coverage; the local Linux full-volume test passed.\n- Permanent corpus covers both sides of batching, checkpoint, migration, and 128 KiB small-blob thresholds, fresh/reused packed and loose storage, and exact durability/content gates. `benchmark all` ran all 40 boundary cases.\n- Frozen Obrador plugin passed Chain-64/Wide-64 against Nix with eight jobs and fresh stores, all 64 completions and requested contents verified. Latest diagnostic appends decreased 3502→2890 (Chain), 1975→1646 (Wide); checkpoints 58→56 and 31→30.\n\nThe approximately 1 ms per-derivation target is not reached. All six follow-up timing attempts were rejected: five could not obtain a quiet host, and one completed with contamination. No accepted speed comparison is available. macOS graph timings remain unavailable. GitHub-hosted jobs cannot start due to the account billing/spending limit; self-hosted validation runs.\n\n[Report, reproduction commands, source hashes, rejected timing attempts, and raw traces](benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency.md). Historical measured and rebased results remain identified separately. This stays a draft while performance and integration validation remain incomplete.\n","files":[{"path":".github/workflows/pin-journal.yml","additions":54,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/all.py","additions":7,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"benchmarks/checkpoint_trace.py","additions":75,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/manifest.json","additions":9,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"benchmarks/pin_validation.py","additions":113,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency.md","additions":263,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/artifacts.json","additions":6,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/environment.json","additions":17,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/execution.json","additions":55,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/ledger-boundaries.json","additions":773,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/ledger-boundaries.log","additions":20,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/ledger-boundaries.md","additions":37,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/obrador-builds.json","additions":191,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/reports/2026-09-10-pin-latency/all-verification/obrador-builds.log","additions":12,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"be